.TH ODX11 1 "October 2026" "opendisplay-x11 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
odx11 \- use an iPad as a second monitor over USB (OpenDisplay for X11)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B odx11
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B odx11
is the program behind OpenDisplay for X11, an unofficial sender for the
OpenDisplay iPad app. It extends an X11 desktop onto an iPad over the USB
cable. Users normally never run it directly: the settings window is in the
application menu, and the service starts automatically at login.
.PP
The computer needs a free HDMI or DisplayPort socket with nothing plugged in.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B settings
Open the settings window.
.TP
.B run
Run the service in the foreground (for debugging); stop the user service first.
.TP
.B daemon
Run the service, logging for the systemd journal (used by odx11.service).
.TP
.B list
List the iOS devices usbmuxd sees.
.TP
.B autostart
Used at login: hand the session's display to systemd and start the service if enabled.
.TP
.B release
Used when the service stops: unforce any video port odx11 left forced on.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Settings file (default:
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/odx11/config.toml ).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log more detail.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/odx11/config.toml
Settings; every key is documented in
.IR /usr/share/doc/opendisplay-x11/config.example.toml .
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/odx11/state.json
The service's current state, read by the settings window.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
https://github.com/cray2015/opendisplay-x11
